## ELIGIBILITY SECTION

Eligibility rules determine whether a record is eligible to begin business processing.

Only include rules whose outcome decides whether processing should start, continue, or stop.

Eligibility rules may include:

• Record identification

• Validation

• Filtering

• Mandatory business preconditions

• Null/Blank checks

• Active/Inactive checks

• Effective date checks

• Existence checks

• Business conditions that determine eligibility

Do NOT classify workflow retrievals, lookups, joins, or mappings as Eligibility unless they directly determine whether the record is eligible for processing.

If a lookup, retrieval, join, or mapping is executed after eligibility has already been established and is used to support subsequent calculations, comparisons, grouping, ranking, updates, migrations, or trigger decisions, classify it under Computation Rules with operation: lookup.

Eligibility rules never perform calculations, updates, migrations, or workflow processing.
Each eligibility rule must contain:

rule_id:
  operation:
  source_entity:
  description:
  filter:
  condition:
  retrieve:

If a field is unavailable, assign null.


---
Eligibility Example:

Eligibility Check:

rule_id: E001
operation: lookup
source_entity: part
description: Verify that the part is eligible for processing.
filter: segment IS NULL
condition: ecc IS NOT NULL
retrieve:
  - short_part_number





Eligibility Decision Rule

Ask the following question for every business action:

"Does the outcome of this rule determine whether business processing is allowed to begin?"

• YES → Eligibility Check

• NO → Computation Rules


